{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-1394"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of cordage, rope, twine and netting"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "1394"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :textiles/cordage
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :labor-standards :materials-traceability]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :cordage-netting-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "CordageAdvisor ⊣ Cordage & Netting Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS
 COORDINATION actor for cordage/rope/twine/netting manufacturing
 (fibre-twisting machines, braiding machines, winding lines; rope,
 twine and knotted/knotless netting output) -- not direct twisting/
 braiding-line control authority. Four ops (`:log-production-batch` /
 `:schedule-maintenance` / `:flag-safety-concern` /
 `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect :propose` only. Eleven concrete
 governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD invariants:
 propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed proposal-effect
 allowlist (no direct twisting/braiding-machine or winding-line
 control), permanent direct-operate block, independent equipment
 verification/registration before maintenance scheduling, independent
 batch verification/registration before shipment coordination,
 independent shipment-volume recompute against the batch's own logged
 length, double-schedule guard, quality-grade validation,
 breaking-strength-test plausibility validation, and defect-rate
 plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging (equipment-safety /
 quality-defect) ALWAYS escalates to a human plant supervisor;
 `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and
 only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
